## 📋 METADATA REQUIREMENTS

### **Jokaiselle sivulle metadata** (Metadata for every page)
Every page must include complete metadata with the following structure:

#### **Required Metadata Fields**
- **title**: Page title (60 characters max)
- **description**: Meta description (160 characters max)
- **openGraph**: Open Graph tags for social sharing
- **alternates.canonical**: Canonical URL for language versions

### **Metadata Implementation**
```tsx
// SEO component structure
<SEO 
  title={t('seo.pageTitle')}
  description={t('seo.pageDescription')}
  canonical={`${baseUrl}/${locale}${pathname}`}
  alternates={{
    'en': `${baseUrl}/en${pathname}`,
    'fi': `${baseUrl}/fi${pathname}`
  }}
  openGraph={{
    title: t('seo.ogTitle'),
    description: t('seo.ogDescription'),
    image: `${baseUrl}/api/og?title=${encodeURIComponent(t('seo.ogTitle'))}`,
    url: `${baseUrl}/${locale}${pathname}`,
    type: 'website',
    locale: locale === 'fi' ? 'fi_FI' : 'en_US'
  }}
/>
```

### **Meta Tag Examples**
```tsx
// Required meta tags
<title>{title}</title>
<meta name="description" content={description} />
<link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />

// Open Graph tags
<meta property="og:title" content={openGraph.title} />
<meta property="og:description" content={openGraph.description} />
<meta property="og:image" content={openGraph.image} />
<meta property="og:url" content={openGraph.url} />
<meta property="og:type" content={openGraph.type} />
<meta property="og:locale" content={openGraph.locale} />

// Language alternates
<link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href={alternates.en} />
<link rel="alternate" hreflang="fi" href={alternates.fi} />
```

## 🖼️ OG-IMAGE GENERATION

### **Luo OG-kuva reitillä /api/og** (Create OG image at route /api/og)
Generate dynamic Open Graph images using brand colors and typography.

### **OG Image API Route**
```typescript
// /api/og/route.ts
import { ImageResponse } from 'next/og';

export async function GET(request: Request) {
  const { searchParams } = new URL(request.url);
  const title = searchParams.get('title') || 'Lyyli.io';
  
  return new ImageResponse(
    (
      <div
        style={{
          background: 'linear-gradient(135deg, #2F5D50 0%, #A7D6D1 100%)',
          width: '1200',
          height: '630',
          display: 'flex',
          flexDirection: 'column',
          alignItems: 'center',
          justifyContent: 'center',
          padding: '60px',
        }}
      >
        <div
          style={{
            fontFamily: 'Playfair Display',
            fontSize: '72px',
            fontWeight: 'bold',
            color: '#FFFFFF',
            textAlign: 'center',
            lineHeight: '1.2',
            marginBottom: '40px',
          }}
        >
          {title}
        </div>
        <div
          style={{
            fontFamily: 'Inter',
            fontSize: '32px',
            color: '#F7EBEB',
            textAlign: 'center',
            maxWidth: '800px',
          }}
        >
          Professional service company communication platform
        </div>
      </div>
    ),
    {
      width: 1200,
      height: 630,
    }
  );
}
```

### **OG Image Requirements**
- **Dimensions**: 1200×630px (Facebook/LinkedIn standard)
- **Brand Colors**: Forest Green (#2F5D50) and Muted Turquoise (#A7D6D1)
- **Typography**: Playfair Display for headings, Inter for body text
- **Dynamic Content**: Generate based on page title parameter
- **Performance**: Optimize for fast generation and caching

## 🤖 ROBOTS.TXT & SITEMAP.XML

### **robots.txt + sitemap.xml pidetään ajan tasalla** (Keep robots.txt and sitemap.xml up to date)
Maintain current robots.txt and sitemap.xml files, updating when new routes are added.

### **Robots.txt Implementation**
```txt
# /public/robots.txt
User-agent: *
Allow: /

# Sitemap
Sitemap: https://lyyli.io/sitemap.xml

# Disallow admin and API routes
Disallow: /admin/
Disallow: /api/
Disallow: /_next/

# Allow important routes
Allow: /features/
Allow: /pricing/
Allow: /blog/
Allow: /help/
```

### **Sitemap.xml Generation**
```typescript
// /app/sitemap.ts
import { MetadataRoute } from 'next';

export default function sitemap(): MetadataRoute.Sitemap {
  const baseUrl = 'https://lyyli.io';
  
  return [
    {
      url: baseUrl,
      lastModified: new Date(),
      changeFrequency: 'weekly',
      priority: 1,
    },
    {
      url: `${baseUrl}/features`,
      lastModified: new Date(),
      changeFrequency: 'monthly',
      priority: 0.8,
    },
    {
      url: `${baseUrl}/pricing`,
      lastModified: new Date(),
      changeFrequency: 'monthly',
      priority: 0.8,
    },
    {
      url: `${baseUrl}/about`,
      lastModified: new Date(),
      changeFrequency: 'monthly',
      priority: 0.6,
    },
    {
      url: `${baseUrl}/blog`,
      lastModified: new Date(),
      changeFrequency: 'weekly',
      priority: 0.7,
    },
    {
      url: `${baseUrl}/contact`,
      lastModified: new Date(),
      changeFrequency: 'monthly',
      priority: 0.6,
    },
    // Finnish versions
    {
      url: `${baseUrl}/fi`,
      lastModified: new Date(),
      changeFrequency: 'weekly',
      priority: 1,
    },
    {
      url: `${baseUrl}/fi/features`,
      lastModified: new Date(),
      changeFrequency: 'monthly',
      priority: 0.8,
    },
    // Add more routes as they're created
  ];
}
```

### **Sitemap Maintenance**
- **Automatic Updates**: Update sitemap when new routes are added
- **Priority Setting**: Set appropriate priorities for different page types
- **Change Frequency**: Update change frequency based on content type
- **Language Versions**: Include both English and Finnish versions

## 📝 HEADING HIERARCHY

### **Heading-hierarkia: 1 × H1 / sivu; looginen H2–H3** (Heading hierarchy: 1 × H1 per page; logical H2–H3)

### **Heading Structure Rules**
- **H1**: Only one per page, main page title
- **H2**: Major section headings (2-4 per page)
- **H3**: Subsection headings (4-8 per page)
- **H4+**: Use sparingly for minor divisions

### **Heading Implementation**
```tsx
// Correct heading hierarchy
<h1 className="font-playfair text-4xl text-forest mb-6">
  Main page title
</h1>

<section>
  <h2 className="font-playfair text-3xl text-forest mb-4">
    Major section heading
  </h2>
  
  <div>
    <h3 className="font-playfair text-2xl text-forest mb-3">
      Subsection heading
    </h3>
    <p>Content...</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 className="font-playfair text-3xl text-forest mb-4">
    Another major section
  </h2>
  {/* Content */}
</section>
```

### **Heading Best Practices**
- **Semantic Structure**: Use headings for content organization, not styling
- **Keyword Placement**: Include relevant keywords in H1 and H2 tags
- **Consistent Styling**: Apply brand typography rules to all headings
- **Accessibility**: Ensure proper heading order for screen readers

